;; C++'s print level's divergences (doc/cpp/CPP-SURVEY.md, "As built: CX10 (write-ahead)"; bin/repr-cpp roundtrip): the classes
;; of test/repr/cpp/roundtrip-known.edn (CX10, generated from its :classes, their texts; the kinds chosen at CX10: a judge's
;; property by design, the converter's and the printer's open cases deferred) and the oracle's two recorded verdicts
;; (roundtrip-oracle.edn, CP130 (c)), in test/goi/divergences.edn's format. A case is CORPUS/NAME (CP127 (b)), its reason
;; "CLASS: the class's text" (bin/reap's reader :cpp-roundtrip). Read with the Clojure reader.
[
 {:id :gxx-objects-location
  :title "g++ -O0's code depends on positions inside a function: the AST and clang's objects are equal, g++'s objects differ"
  :kind :design
  :why "g++ -O0's code depends on positions inside a function (a coroutine's frame, -fcompare-debug, asan and the like): the AST and clang's objects are equal, g++'s objects differ (CP48; C3b's :objects): level 4's g++ half cannot hold for a print whose lines move"
  :decided "CP48 (the user, 2026-10-30); the kind CX10's"
  :match [#"^known gxx-objects-location:"]}
 {:id :print-rejected
  :title "the print does not compile: a construct the converter or the printer gets wrong"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "the print does not compile: dependent names, abbreviated templates, unexpanded packs, decomposition corners, a #define inside an #if dropped (CP45): the converter's and the printer's open cases (CX5 and on)"
  :decided "CP45; the kind CX10's"
  :match [#"^known print-rejected:"]}
 {:id :forms-differ
  :title "the print compiles but reads back to other forms"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "the print compiles but reads back to other forms (a spelling the converter does not keep the same way twice): the converter's open cases"
  :decided "CX4; the kind CX10's"
  :match [#"^known forms-differ:"]}
 {:id :ast-differs
  :title "the print compiles to another AST"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "the print compiles to another AST: isUsed lost through canonical template arguments, a parenthesized type (int (T::*)), the line of a __LINE__ in a structured node, deduction guides, implicit members: the printer's open cases"
  :decided "CX4; the kind CX10's"
  :match [#"^known ast-differs:"]}
 {:id :objects-differ
  :title "the AST is equal, clang's objects differ"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "the AST is equal, clang's objects differ (since CP95 (b) and review 123's F2 only gxx-dg/ext/arm-fp16/arm-fp16-ops-1.C is recorded so, an improvement until gxx-dg-every-10's next --record-results)"
  :decided "CP95 (b); the kind CX10's"
  :match [#"^known objects-differ:"]}
 {:id :read-crash
  :title "the read (the converter or the printer) throws, before any level"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "the read throws before any level (no file is in it since CP131 (b))"
  :decided "CP131 (b); the kind CX10's"
  :match [#"^known read-crash:"]}
 {:id :rejected-differs
  :title "the oracle rejects the file, the native reader reads it: level 1 or R differs"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "clang rejects the file, the native reader reads and prints it (CPR1, doc/cpp/PRINT-DESIGN-REVIEW.md): the print read again natively gives other forms (level 1), or the print does not fail like the original (level R: clang's and g++'s errors by message, positions dropped): the native parser's, the converter's and the printer's open cases"
  :decided "CPR1 (a), CPR2 (a) (the user, 2026-11-05)"
  :match [#"^known rejected-differs:"]}
 {:id :oracle-rejects
  :title "clang, the oracle, rejects the file and the native reader cannot read it"
  :kind :design
  :why "since CPR1 (2026-11-05) only a file the native reader refuses or throws on (the others are read natively and judged at level R: pass or rejected-differs); clang rejects the file with its own diagnostics (a dg-error test, a g++ extension or a target clang does not take): the oracle-fed reader (CP3 (a)) has no AST to convert; recorded by name per corpus (roundtrip-oracle.edn, CP130 (c)); the error tests are the read level's, judged on rejection and position by CX9's dg check"
  :decided "CP3 (a), CP130 (c); the kind CX10's; narrowed by CPR1 (a), CPR2 (a) (the user, 2026-11-05)"
  :match [#"^oracle-rejects oracle-rejects:"]}
 {:id :oracle-fails
  :title "the oracle's dump failed (a timeout or a crash)"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "the oracle's dump failed, recorded by name and kind (CP130 (c)): gxx-dg/cpp0x/pr104668.C's dump times out, gxx-dg/modules/target-aarch64-1_b.C's clang crashes; a longer budget or a fixed clang may close them"
  :decided "CP130 (c); the kind CX10's"
  :match [#"^oracle-fails oracle-fails:"]}
 {:id :read-refused
  :title "the converter refuses the file (a declaration it has no form for whose text is not plain)"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "the converter refuses the file (a declaration it has no form for whose text is not plain: clang's dump gives it no end, or it spans another file; CX9's modules part, test/repr/cpp/roundtrip-known.edn): the converter's open cases"
  :decided "CX9; the kind cppi-check's (2026-11-05), as the read level's class read-refused of test/cpp/divergences-dg.edn"
  :match [#"^known read-refused:"]}
 ;; cpp-90 (the user's decision of 2026-11-07): the own judge's rule classes (bin/repr-cpp roundtrip --judge own, arbace.repr.cpp.rtcheck)
 {:id :native-refused
  :title "the native parser refuses the file (no clang at read time)"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "the native parser (CX11, doc/cpp/NATIVE.md) declines a construct it does not read yet, or the file is ill-formed in a way it stops at; under the own judge the file has no oracle read to fall back on, so it is the parser's gap"
  :decided "cpp-90 (the own judge)"
  :match [#"^known native-refused:"]}
 {:id :full-differs
  :title "mode :full's print is not the original's bytes"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "level 5: the :full read written as .ae text, read back and printed differs from the source (a spelling, a layout or a comment the :full forms do not keep)"
  :decided "cpp-90 (the own judge)"
  :match [#"^known full-differs:"]}
]
